(Arduino is an open-source electronics platform based on easy-to-use hardware and software. At its heart lies a) Tj
T* (microcontroller뾞 compact integrated circuit designed to govern a specific operation in an embedded system. ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Unlike a microprocessor \(found in PCs and smartphones\) which requires external RAM, ROM, and I/O peripherals to function, a) Tj
T* (microcontroller integrates the CPU core, volatile memory \(SRAM\), non-volatile program memory \(Flash\), rewritable storage) Tj
T* (\(EEPROM\), and programmable input/output peripherals onto a single monolithic silicon die.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
39.6850393700787407 631.559291338582625 Td
(Arduino UNO Hardware Architecture) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 617.3860629921259715 Td
(The Arduino UNO R3 is built around the Microchip ATmega328P. Key hardware specifications include:) Tj
T* (- Clock Speed: 16 MHz quartz crystal oscillator) Tj
T* (- Flash Memory: 32 KB \(0.5 KB occupied by bootloader\)) Tj
T* (- SRAM: 2 KB \(volatile runtime variables\)) Tj
T* (- EEPROM: 1 KB \(non-volatile persistent storage\)) Tj
T* (- Operating Voltage: 5V DC) Tj
T* (- Recommended Input Voltage \(VIN / Barrel Jack\): 7V - 12V DC) Tj
T* (- Absolute Maximum VIN: 6V - 20V \(beyond 12V causes excessive linear regulator heating\)) Tj
T* (- DC Current per I/O Pin: 20 mA recommended \(40 mA absolute maximum\)) Tj
T* (- DC Current for 3.3V Pin: 50 mA maximum) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
39.6850393700787407 481.323070866141677 Td
(Pinout Taxonomy & Pin Categorization) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 467.1498425196850235 Td
(The Arduino UNO exposes 28 header pins divided into specific functional groups:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1. Digital I/O Pins \(D0 to D13\):) Tj
T* (   Configured via pinMode\(pin, INPUT/OUTPUT\). Logic HIGH represents +5V; logic LOW represents 0V.) Tj
T* (   - D0 \(RX\) & D1 \(TX\): Hardware UART Serial communication. Leave disconnected during USB sketch upload.) Tj
T* (   - D13: Connected to the onboard surface-mount LED through an internal buffer.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2. Pulse Width Modulation \(PWM\) Pins \(~3, ~5, ~6, ~9, ~10, ~11\):) Tj
T* (   Indicated with a tilde \(~\) mark. Provide 8-bit pseudo-analog output \(0 to 255\) using analogWrite\(\) at ~490 Hz \(pins 5 and 6 run) Tj
T* (at ~980 Hz\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3. Analog Input Pins \(A0 to A5\):) Tj
T* (   Read varying analog voltages \(0V to 5V\) using a 10-bit Successive Approximation Analog-to-Digital Converter \(ADC\).) Tj
T* (Resolution: 1024 discrete steps \(0 to 1023\), equaling ~4.88 mV per unit step. Can also serve as digital I/O pins \(D14 to D19\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (4. Power and Ground Pins:) Tj
T* (   - VIN: Raw voltage input when using an external battery \(7-12V\).) Tj
T* (   - 5V: Regulated +5V output from USB or onboard NCP1117 regulator.) Tj
T* (   - 3.3V: Regulated +3.3V supply \(LP2985-33\) for low-voltage sensors.) Tj
T* (   - GND: Ground reference \(0V\). All circuits must share a common ground.) Tj
