(Why Do We Need a Motor Driver?) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 720.0002362204724022 Td
(A digital pin on an Arduino UNO can safely source a maximum of 20 to 40 milliamperes \(mA\) at 5 volts. A standard DC geared) Tj
T* (motor \(such as a 12V TT gearmotor or planetary gearmotor used for lifting platforms\) draws between 300 mA under no-load) Tj
T* (conditions to over 2.5 A when stalled or lifting a load. Connecting a motor directly to an Arduino pin will instantly vaporize the) Tj
T* (output stage transistor of the ATmega328P.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Furthermore, motors are inductive loads. When current through an inductor is suddenly interrupted, magnetic field collapse) Tj
T* (generates a massive reverse voltage spike \(back-EMF: V = -L * di/dt\) that can reach tens or hundreds of volts, destroying) Tj
T* (unshielded digital electronics. A motor driver isolates the microcontroller, provides flyback diode protection, and switches heavy) Tj
T* (currents using an external power source.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
39.6850393700787407 595.8427559055116944 Td
(The H-Bridge Topology & Truth Table) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 581.6695275590550409 Td
(An H-Bridge consists of four solid-state switching elements \(BJTs or MOSFETs\) arranged in the shape of an 'H' around the) Tj
T* (motor:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (- Forward Rotation: Q1 \(top-left\) and Q4 \(bottom-right\) closed. Current flows Left to Right through the motor.) Tj
T* (- Reverse Rotation: Q2 \(top-right\) and Q3 \(bottom-left\) closed. Current flows Right to Left through the motor.) Tj
T* (- High-Impedance Coast: All switches open. Motor freewheels.) Tj
T* (- Dynamic Braking: Q3 and Q4 \(or Q1 and Q2\) closed. Both motor terminals shorted together, dissipating kinetic energy as) Tj
T* (reverse magnetic braking.) Tj
T* (- Shoot-Through \(Catastrophic Fault\): Closing Q1 and Q3 simultaneously creates a direct short from +V to GND. The L298N) Tj
T* (internal logic prevents shoot-through by hardware interlocks.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
39.6850393700787407 445.6065354330708033 Td
(L298N Terminal Configuration & Jumper Rules) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 431.4333070866140929 Td
(1. 12V Power Terminal: External DC supply for motors \(7V - 35V\). For our lifting platform, a 12V 3A DC power source is) Tj
T* (connected here.) Tj
T* (2. GND Terminal: Common ground reference. MUST be connected to BOTH the 12V external power supply ground and the) Tj
T* (Arduino UNO GND pin.) Tj
T* (3. 5V Logic Terminal: Powers the internal 78M05 voltage regulator.) Tj
T* (   - If 5V Jumper is ON: Onboard regulator converts external 12V down to 5V to power internal logic. Do NOT connect external) Tj
T* (5V to this pin.) Tj
T* (   - If 5V Jumper is REMOVED \(External motor > 12V\): Onboard regulator is disabled. You must supply +5V from Arduino 5V to) Tj
T* (this pin.) Tj
T* (4. ENA / ENB \(Enable Pins\): Speed control. Removing the jumper cap exposes the pin for an Arduino PWM signal \(0-255\).) Tj
T* (5. IN1, IN2 \(Motor A\) / IN3, IN4 \(Motor B\): Direction control logic pins.) Tj
ET
