(Piezoelectric Ultrasonic Transducers & Working Principle) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 720.0002362204724022 Td
(The HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor utilizes acoustic echolocation to calculate distance without physical contact. The module) Tj
T* (incorporates two aluminum cylindrical transducers:) Tj
T* (1. Transmitter \(T\): Contains a piezoelectric crystal disc that vibrates at 40,000 Hertz \(40 kHz\) when stimulated by high-frequency) Tj
T* (electrical pulses, radiating a focused conical ultrasonic beam into the air.) Tj
T* (2. Receiver \(R\): Contains an identical crystal tuned to 40 kHz. When incoming reflected sound waves strike the diaphragm,) Tj
T* (mechanical stress generates a minute alternating electrical charge, which is amplified and conditioned by onboard LM324) Tj
T* (operational amplifiers.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
39.6850393700787407 619.6537795275589815 Td
(The Time-of-Flight \(ToF\) Physical Formula) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 605.480551181102328 Td
(Distance calculation relies on the speed of sound propagating through air at standard sea-level atmospheric pressure and 20캜:) Tj
T* (␀S␀p␀e␀e␀d␀ ␀o␀f␀ ␀S␀o␀u␀n␀d␀ ␀\(␀c␀\)␀ "H␀ ␀3␀4␀3␀ ␀m␀e␀t␀e␀r␀s␀/␀s␀e␀c␀o␀n␀d␀ ␀=␀ ␀0␀.␀0␀3␀4␀3␀ ␀c␀e␀n␀t␀i␀m␀e␀t␀e␀r␀s␀/␀m␀i␀c␀r␀o␀s␀e␀c␀o␀n␀d␀.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Because the acoustic burst travels outward from the transmitter to the reflective water surface and bounces all the way back to) Tj
T* (the receiver, the total distance traveled is twice the distance to the target:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Distance = \(Time Elapsed * Speed of Sound\) / 2) Tj
T* (Distance \(cm\) = \(Echo Time in 탎 * 0.0343\) / 2) Tj
T* (Simplified: Distance \(cm\) = Echo Time in 탎 / 58.3) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Temperature Compensation Consideration:) Tj
T* (Sound velocity varies with ambient air temperature: c\(T\) = 331.3 + \(0.606 * T\) m/s. In flood conditions where air humidity and) Tj
T* (temperature fluctuate, incorporating a DHT11 or DHT22 temperature sensor refines distance calculations to millimeter accuracy.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
39.6850393700787407 433.7010236220471597 Td
(Water Level Monitoring Strategy in Flood Mitigation) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 419.5277952755905062 Td
(When measuring floodwater depth, the ultrasonic sensor is mounted overhead facing downward into the retention basin or) Tj
T* (foundation channel:) Tj
T* (- Basin Depth \(Baseline Calibration\): e.g., 50 cm from sensor to dry floor.) Tj
T* (- Measured Ultrasonic Distance: The distance from the sensor down to the water surface.) Tj
T* (- Calculated Water Depth: Flood Level = Baseline Calibration - Measured Distance.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (As floodwater rises, the measured distance decreases.) Tj
T* (Example: If the baseline is 50 cm and the sensor reads 15 cm, the floodwater depth is exactly 35 cm. If the critical threshold is) Tj
T* (set to 20 cm depth, an emergency lifting command is triggered immediately.) Tj
