0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
39.6850393700787407 773.8585039370078675 Td
(Module 05: Rain Sensor Module \(FC-37 / YL-83\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.231 0.51 0.965 rg
39.6850393700787407 756.8506299212598378 Td
(Resistive Trace Detection, LM393 Comparator, and Precipitation Telemetry) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
39.6850393700787407 734.1734645669291695 Td
(Electrolytic Resistance Principle of Rain Sensing) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 720.0002362204724022 Td
(The rain sensor system consists of two primary hardware elements:) Tj
T* (1. Sensing Pad: A printed circuit board with interleaved, interdigitated copper/nickel conductive tracks. When dry, air acts as an) Tj
T* (electrical insulator, resulting in near-infinite resistance \(several megaohms\). When precipitation falls, water droplets contain) Tj
T* (dissolved minerals and ions that act as an electrolyte, creating conductive bridges between adjacent tracks and dramatically) Tj
T* (lowering electrical resistance.) Tj
T* (2. Signal Conditioning Module: Features an LM393 dual differential voltage comparator, a sensitivity trim potentiometer, status) Tj
T* (LEDs, and output headers.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
39.6850393700787407 619.6537795275589815 Td
(Understanding AO \(Analog\) and DO \(Digital\) Outputs) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 605.480551181102328 Td
(The sensor board provides two distinct output channels:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1. Analog Output \(AO\):) Tj
T* (   Provides an analog voltage proportional to the electrical resistance across the sensor tracks. In an Arduino with a 5V) Tj
T* (reference:) Tj
T* (   - Completely Dry: AO reads 1000 - 1023 \(~5.0V, high resistance\).) Tj
T* (   - Light Drizzle / Condensation: AO reads 600 - 800 \(~3.0V - 4.0V\).) Tj
T* (   - Moderate Rainfall: AO reads 400 - 600 \(~2.0V - 3.0V\).) Tj
T* (   - Heavy Downpour / Submersion: AO reads < 350 \(< 1.7V, high conductivity\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2. Digital Output \(DO\):) Tj
T* (   The onboard LM393 compares the sensor voltage with a reference voltage set by the multi-turn potentiometer.) Tj
T* (   - When moisture exceeds the potentiometer threshold, DO flips from HIGH \(5V\) to LOW \(0V\), triggering an active-low) Tj
T* (hardware interrupt or digital read.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
39.6850393700787407 421.7955118110235162 Td
(Preventing Galvanic & Electrolytic Corrosion) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 407.6222834645668058 Td
(A critical engineering challenge with resistive rain sensors is galvanic oxidation. If DC current continuously flows through the wet) Tj
T* (nickel tracks, electrolysis rapidly oxidizes the metal, causing traces to corrode and disintegrate within days or weeks of) Tj
T* (deployment.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Professional Solution:) Tj
T* (Do not connect the rain sensor VCC pin permanently to the Arduino 5V power rail. Instead, connect VCC to a digital I/O pin \(e.g.,) Tj
T* (Pin 7\). Set the pin HIGH only 10 milliseconds before taking an analog reading, sample the voltage, and immediately pull the pin) Tj
T* (LOW \(0V\). This eliminates continuous galvanic current, extending sensor lifespan by over 500x.) Tj
ET
