BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
39.6850393700787407 737.0081102362204319 Td
(Context: A heavy monsoon thunderstorm begins in the catchment zone. The rain sensor AO drops sharply to 320 \(indicating intense) Tj
T* (downpour\). However, the overhead HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor reports a distance of 38 cm \(indicating only 2 cm of ground moisture in) Tj
T* (the drainage gutter, well below the 15 cm danger threshold\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.086 0.396 0.204 rg
39.6850393700787407 699.0238582677164914 Td
(Optimal Protocol: Sound a pre-warning status, keep the house on the ground, and increase ultrasonic polling frequency to monitor depth trends.) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 684.8506299212598378 Td
(Rationale: Modern civil flood barriers implement multi-sensor redundancy. Rain sensors provide early weather awareness, but actual) Tj
T* (physical elevation should only occur when hydrological accumulation \(water level depth\) is verified by the acoustic or hydrostatic depth) Tj
T* (sensor.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.145 0.388 0.922 rg
39.6850393700787407 635.5277952755905062 Td
(Scenario 02: Water Level Suddenly Surges Past Critical Threshold) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
39.6850393700787407 621.3545669291338527 Td
(Context: A flash flood surge occurs following a riverbank breach. The ultrasonic sensor detects water rising rapidly from 4 cm to 18 cm) Tj
T* (within 20 seconds, exceeding the 15 cm critical threshold.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.086 0.396 0.204 rg
39.6850393700787407 594.1419685039370506 Td
(Optimal Protocol: Sound buzzer & illuminate Red LED -> Disengage servo safety locks -> Command L298N forward lifting -> Monitor upper limit switch.) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 579.9687401574802834 Td
(Rationale: Sequential interlock control is fundamental to mechatronics. Actuators must follow a strict non-conflicting dependency graph:) Tj
T* (Annunciation -> Unlock -> Drive -> Limit Stop -> Lock.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.145 0.388 0.922 rg
39.6850393700787407 541.4175590551180903 Td
(Scenario 03: Ultrasonic Sensor Detects Erroneous Distance During Waves) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
39.6850393700787407 527.2443307086614368 Td
(Context: Violent wind causes turbulent waves in the flood basin. Over 5 seconds, the ultrasonic sensor returns: [14cm, 0cm, 15cm,) Tj
T* (298cm, 14.5cm]. The 0cm and 298cm readings are acoustic reflection timeouts caused by wave tilt reflecting sound away from the) Tj
T* (receiver.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.086 0.396 0.204 rg
39.6850393700787407 489.2600787401574962 Td
(Optimal Protocol: Implement a median filter \(e.g. sample 5 values, discard min/max outliers, sort and take median\) before passing to the state machine.) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 475.0868503937007858 Td
(Rationale: Digital signal processing \(DSP\) techniques such as running median filters, moving averages, and range-clamping are) Tj
T* (mandatory when fielding ultrasonic sensors over liquid surfaces subject to turbulence.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.145 0.388 0.922 rg
39.6850393700787407 436.5356692913385928 Td
(Scenario 04: House Reaches its Upper Lifting Limit) Tj
